# Security — Auth & AuthZ

## Required

- Authenticate before mutating or reading user-owned resources
- Derive `UserId` from server identity — never trust client-supplied owner ids
- Application routes must enforce ownership (prefer 404 over leaking existence)
- Cookies holding credentials: `HttpOnly`; `Secure` in production; set `SameSite` deliberately
- Never store access tokens in `localStorage`

## Review checklist

- [ ] Unauthenticated calls get 401
- [ ] Cross-user id access blocked (IDOR test)
- [ ] Password hashes only — no plaintext
- [ ] No secrets in logs or committed files

## Teach moment

If editing auth, ask the learner to explain **one** of: session vs JWT, or why HttpOnly matters, before closing the task.
